&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Zscaler (NASDAQ: ZS) accelerates digital transformation so customers can be more agile, efficient, resilient, and secure. The Zscaler Zero Trust Exchange™️ platform protects thousands of customers from cyberattacks and data loss by securely connecting users, devices, and applications in any location. Distributed across 160+ public exchanges globally and thousands of private exchanges at the edge, the SASE-based Zero Trust Exchange is the world’s largest in-line cloud security platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the future of work is Human + AI and are building an AI-native enterprise where human potential is amplified by machine intelligence to solve the world’s hardest security challenges. Driven by deep customer obsession, we are committed to the mission, outcome, and to each other. We bring these commitments to life through three core behaviors: ownership and collaboration, trust through outcomes and impact, and a challenge culture with ongoing feedback. Ready to make an impact at the company pioneering security transformation in the AI era? Join us at Zscaler.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Principal Product Specialist – Browser Security to join our team. This is a Hybrid (Bangalore) role, reporting to the Director, Threat Researcher in the Engineering department. Zscaler is seeking a hands-on technical specialist to drive customer adoption and secure enterprise sales wins.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this technical, customer-facing role, you will collaborate with Sales, Product, and Engineering to lead product walkthroughs, technical workshops, proof-of-value engagements, deployments, and live troubleshooting. You will translate browser security capabilities into clear business outcomes for CISOs, security leaders, and architects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Zscaler’s Browser Security technical specialist, leading customer discovery, demos, solution deep dives, and architecture discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own or support POCs / POVs, including success criteria definition, test planning, execution support, and outcome validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers design and validate browser-layer security controls and use cases, including threat prevention, protection against browser-delivered attacks, in-browser data protection, secure workflows, and policy-based browser controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with security architects, SOC teams, endpoint teams, application security teams, and CISO-level stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams (Sales, Product, Engineering, Customer Success) to provide deployment guidance, policy recommendations, and troubleshooting during customer evaluations, supporting US East timezone calls as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Success Profile)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You act like an owner, driven by a passion for the mission and a strong bias for action. You navigate seamlessly between high-level strategy and hands-on execution while taking full responsibility for outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a high-trust collaborator who thrives in a team-first environment. You foster open dialogue by giving and receiving constructive feedback with clarity, respect, and candor to build lasting trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are customer-obsessed, building deep empathy for internal and external stakeholders to solve their real-world security challenges. You champion user needs from discovery to resolution, measuring success by customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are driven by innovation and energized by solving complex technical challenges. You bring curiosity to understanding browser security architecture and continuously seek scalable, secure solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You lead with integrity and high accountability, consistently aligning your actions with your commitments to foster transparency and trust across cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of AI/ML technologies and experience leveraging, securing, or positioning AI-driven solutions to optimize outcomes within your functional domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–12 years of cybersecurity experience (web security, pentesting, or product specialization) within a security vendor, VAR, systems integrator, or enterprise security team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with browser security controls and a strong understanding of web threat prevention, client-side attack surfaces, browser exploitation, phishing defense, in-browser data protection, and secure enterprise browsing, along with browser-related endpoint and network controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience driving enterprise engagements (POCs, POVs, deployments) and delivering technical workshops and walkthroughs to both executive and practitioner audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of web and security fundamentals, including HTTP/HTTPS, SSL/TLS, DNS, browser architecture, web threats, enterprise access controls, and data protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional collaborator comfortable with direct customer interaction, live troubleshooting, hands-on technical problem solving, and supporting US East timezone meetings as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out (Preferred Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to leverage AI technologies and workflows to drive measurable operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering or product development experience with browser controls, web inspection, threat detection, telemetry, policy enforcement engines, and endpoint agents or extensions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in applied security roles, including security research, red teaming, penetration testing, threat/malware analysis, or application security engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-SK3&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-HYBRID&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;At Zscaler, we are committed to building a team that reflects the communities we serve and the customers we work with. We foster an inclusive environment that values all backgrounds and perspectives, emphasizing collaboration and belonging. Join us in our mission to make doing business seamless and secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Benefits program is one of the most important ways we support our employees. Zscaler proudly offers comprehensive and inclusive benefits to meet the diverse needs of our employees and their families throughout their life stages, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;has-nudge&quot; data-nudge-id=&quot;5eb9419b-6a4d-4451-bfa6-e2eb96084be0&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Various health plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off plans for vacation and sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office perks, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;has-nudge&quot; data-nudge-id=&quot;5eb9419b-6a4d-4451-bfa6-e2eb96084be0&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Learn more about Zscaler&#39;s hybrid working model and benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zscaler.com/candidate-resource-hub&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this role, you adhere to applicable laws, regulations, and Zscaler policies, including those related to security and privacy standards and guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Zscaler is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all individuals. We strive to create a workplace where employees are treated with respect and have the chance to succeed. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy or related medical conditions), age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. &lt;em&gt;See more information by clicking on the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;link.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Transparency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler complies with all applicable federal, state, and local pay transparency rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler is committed to providing reasonable support (called accommodations or adjustments) in our recruiting processes for candidates who are differently abled, have long term conditions, mental health conditions or sincerely held religious beliefs, or who are neurodivergent or require pregnancy-related support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
